# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files. Recursive, so it covers `backend/.env` too — that file holds every
# provider credential and must never reach a repository.
.env*
# The templates are the exception: they carry names and comments, never values.
# Without these two lines the pattern above would swallow them and a fresh
# clone would have nothing to copy from.
!.env.example
!backend/.env.example

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# Railway CLI working directories. `.railway` holds the local project link;
# `.railway-config-pull-*` is scaffolding a failed `config pull` leaves behind.
.railway
.railway-config-pull-*

# Scratch copies made while bisecting a deploy problem.
*.bak

# Marketing renders. Launch films and feature clips are published to social,
# not served by the app, and each one is megabytes that would sit in history
# forever. Assets the app actually loads live under `public/` and are committed
# — `public/loader.mp4` is required at runtime, so it is deliberately not
# covered here. Only the repository root is ignored.
/*.mp4
/*.mov

# Assistant entrypoint. It contains one line — a pointer at AGENTS.md, which is
# the real guide — so it is a local convenience rather than part of the
# project. Kept on disk, out of the repository.
CLAUDE.md
